<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Athina's entitlements, for the development bundle (scripts/bundle.sh) and the
	direct-download release (scripts/release.sh) alike. Keep it to what the app
	does today, each key with the reason it is here.

	The release runs under the hardened runtime, which Developer ID notarization
	requires. Nothing else Athina does needs an exception to it: screen capture,
	Accessibility, and speech recognition are privacy permissions the person
	grants, not entitlements; the Carbon hotkey, the login keychain, the network
	(no App Sandbox), Vision, and the SQLite shim linked into the binary need none;
	and the release will sign the libraries the app embeds, such as the local
	speech models' runtime (whisper.cpp for Whisper and Parakeet), with the app's
	own team, so library validation passes without disabling it. No JIT, no
	unsigned executable memory, no Apple Events.

	The App Sandbox is off. The Mac App Store edition, the Xcode project's Athina
	App Store target (project.yml), signs with Resources/Athina.app-store.entitlements
	instead: the key below plus com.apple.security.app-sandbox and the sandbox
	entitlements the app needs inside it. A key added here that the sandboxed app
	needs goes there too.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		The talk-back shortcut listens through AVAudioEngine. The hardened runtime
		refuses microphone input without this, whatever the person granted in
		System Settings. The unhardened development build does not need it.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
